{
  "$meta": {
    "name": "FA Lens Design Tokens",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "updated": "2026-09-09",
    "identity": "Optics. The tool is a lens: it brings truth into focus. LIGHT default for readability (decision 2026-09-09); dark is a full twin, not an afterthought. One cool accent (Iris) for navigation and interaction; one warm Flare reserved for the single active thing. Together they mimic lens chromatic aberration (cyan/orange fringes).",
    "rules": [
      "Components never use raw hex. Only tokens.",
      "Hue budget per screen: accent + ok/warn/crit. Flare only on the primary button and the running state. Info only inside a badge.",
      "Text on a tinted (-soft) fill uses the matching -text token, never the strong color. Strong colors are for fills, dots, bars, and large display numbers only.",
      "Light is the default theme. Every color has a dark twin with the same role and similar contrast.",
      "Density is a mode: comfortable (default) and dense (toggle, remembered per user). Never hardcode a row height.",
      "Uppercase letter-spaced labels only in table headers. Card labels are sentence case.",
      "Animate only transform, opacity, filter, stroke-dashoffset. Never layout properties."
    ]
  },
